<title>INDIA: Indian soybean ends up on demand from processors.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean ends up on demand from processors.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian soybean ended Tuesday firm on good demand from processing plants, traders said.</p>
<p>They said prices rose 50-150 rupees per tonne in light trade and a firm undertone.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices dropped 400 rupees per tonne on selling by processing plants and refineries in brisk trade and an easy undertone, traders said.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices were firm on international trends, they said. Soymeal yellow was $305-306 per tonne FAS (Free Alongside Ship) in export. Rapeseed extraction was $119-120 per tonne FAS (Free Along Ship) for export. Rapeseed extraction was 4,050-4,100 rupees per tonne in FOR (Free on Rail) condition. Business volumes were dull and the undertone firm, traders said.</p>
